2.1.	Module Learning Outcomes (LOs)
By the end of this module, participants will be able to:
1.	Compare and apply a range of sophisticated and appropriate machine learning techniques to solve organisational problems.
2.	Critically analyse, interpret, and evaluate complex information from diverse datasets to predict and infer likely outcomes. 
3.	Devise and direct an impartial, scientific, and hypothesis-driven approach to a work-based challenge, using rigorous data analysis methods.
4.	Articulate data-driven conclusions in an appropriate manner.
5.	Defend recommendations to decision makers, linking machine learning outcomes to  the achievement of your organisation’s goals.
